\begin_layout Exercise*
Let \begin_inset Formula $X=\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}$\end_inset
 and \begin_inset Formula $B(p,w)=\{x\in X:p\cdot x\leq w\}$\end_inset
, where \begin_inset Formula $p\gg0$\end_inset
 and \begin_inset Formula $w>0$\end_inset
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Exercise*
(a) Prove that \begin_inset Formula $B(\lambda p,\lambda w)=B(p,w)$\end_inset
 for every \begin_inset Formula $\lambda>0$\end_inset
. Explain why every demand correspondence generated by preference maximization is homogeneous of degree zero in \begin_inset Formula $(p,w)$\end_inset
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Exercise*
(b) Suppose preferences are locally nonsatiated. Prove that every chosen bundle satisfies Walras' law, \begin_inset Formula $p\cdot x=w$\end_inset
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Exercise*
(c) For \begin_inset Formula $u(x)=x_{1}^{\alpha}x_{2}^{1-\alpha}$\end_inset
 with \begin_inset Formula $0<\alpha<1$\end_inset
, derive Marshallian demand and verify both properties directly.
\end_layout

